WEBVTT

00:00:00.088 --> 00:00:05.300
Global Config holds shared framework configuration credential references and

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.762
provider settings Choose the intended vault mode and verify its runtime

00:00:09.762 --> 00:00:15.175
support Keep vault material and backups protected Credential groups now

00:00:15.175 --> 00:00:19.625
organize local definitions by datacenter and cluster with shared-service

00:00:19.625 --> 00:00:24.620
groups for references used across environments Use search and purpose labels

00:00:24.738 --> 00:00:29.558
to find the intended reference Local secret values remain masked in the list

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:35.200
Grouping is organizational metadata Credential resolution remains flat a

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:40.075
group does not create a new reference namespace Removing a group does not

00:00:40.075 --> 00:00:45.162
remove its credentials Review administrator metadata changes carefully and

00:00:45.162 --> 00:00:49.395
verify the actual target and purpose before using a reference

00:00:49.754 --> 00:00:54.029
Create a clear reference for each target account or password transition.

00:00:54.429 --> 00:00:57.817
The username must match the account requested by the script.

00:00:58.217 --> 00:01:02.267
Use separate references for new local administrators and independent

00:01:02.279 --> 00:01:05.192
nonempty passwords where validation requires them.

00:01:05.592 --> 00:01:07.767
A reference name is not a password.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:13.154
Validate resolution without printing secret values into logs, tickets

00:01:13.304 --> 00:01:14.779
or tutorial screenshots.

00:01:15.921 --> 00:01:21.083
Config Files remains the shared library for workflow script pipeline and

00:01:21.083 --> 00:01:26.303
recovery inputs Open the intended file and inspect its targets before saving

00:01:26.583 --> 00:01:31.183
Retain reviewed recovery versions Organize files using datacenter and

00:01:31.183 --> 00:01:36.196
cluster groups shared credential groups and purpose labels Search and scoped

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:41.246
workflow or pipeline pickers help narrow the list Group labels do not rename

00:01:41.246 --> 00:01:46.383
a file rewrite its Y A M L or change execution

00:01:46.383 --> 00:01:51.283
references Choose the exact saved filename and confirm its content before

00:01:51.283 --> 00:01:56.616
execution Restoring or editing a file changes desired input

00:01:56.958 --> 00:02:01.346
it does not reverse target-side changes If the file belongs to a reviewed

00:02:01.346 --> 00:02:06.741
recovery baseline capture and review a new revision when its content changes

00:02:07.116 --> 00:02:11.341
In YAML Studio choose the correct template family and generator.

00:02:11.741 --> 00:02:15.841
Complete the fields, generate the document and inspect validation,

00:02:16.329 --> 00:02:18.504
mapping and adapter-readiness findings.

00:02:18.904 --> 00:02:23.166
Resolve missing references or unsupported properties before saving.

00:02:23.554 --> 00:02:28.191
A successful YAML save is not execution approval, a live connection

00:02:28.191 --> 00:02:30.004
test or a completed deployment.

00:02:30.404 --> 00:02:33.966
Open the corresponding execution workflow for those next steps.

00:02:35.141 --> 00:02:40.329
Before execution, compare the saved YAML, action, target and credential

00:02:40.329 --> 00:02:42.129
references with the approved change.

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:45.454
Approval can be bound to exact content and filename.

00:02:45.841 --> 00:02:49.179
Editing the document afterward can invalidate that binding.

00:02:49.566 --> 00:02:52.516
Never loosen policy to make changed content run.

00:02:52.916 --> 00:02:57.516
Keep sanitized configuration hashes and job identifiers so another

00:02:57.516 --> 00:03:01.166
operator can reconcile what was requested and what actually executed.
